easured by a shake flask method. An aqueous solution (1.0 mL) of several compounds of equal concentration was mixed with n-octanol, centrifuged at room temperature for 4 h, centrifuged at 2500 rpm, and centrifuged for 15 min to separate the different phases. The solutes in the liquid phase were separated and the platinum content in the initial and final phases was determined by ICP-MS. The log PO/W was calculated using the following equation: log PO/W = log [(Ptinitial - Ptfinal)/ Ptfinal]"}]}